// std/core/deep_copy: a copy of a value that shares nothing it can write.
//
// The runtime walks the value the way the collector does, by the layout of each
// type, and copies every object it reaches once: two references to one object
// reach one copy, and a cycle stays a cycle. A string is immutable and stays
// shared, and so do the values of `std/task` that tasks share by design: a copy
// of a struct holding a task joins the same task.

module "std/core"

/// A copy of `value` that shares nothing it can write: every struct and array it
/// reaches is copied, once.
///
/// Two references to one object of `value` are two references to one copy, and a
/// cycle stays a cycle. A view of an array is copied as an array of the elements
/// it shows. Strings stay shared, being immutable, and so do the values of
/// `std/task` that tasks share, a task among them.
///
/// A function value stops the program, since what the function captured cannot
/// be copied.
///
/// `.clone()` on an array copies the array only: its elements stay shared.
///
/// @param value  the value to copy.
/// @example
///   rows :: [[1, 2], [3]]
///   copy :: rows.deep_copy()
///   copy[0].push(9)
///   rows[0]   // [1, 2]
@intrinsic export deep_copy :: fn<T>(value: T) -> T
